A||||4||crzyone||Headlight problem||||1||
Z||000000||crzyone||03-18-2001||01:44 AM||||Hey there<P>Maybe someone has had this problem before...  when I turn on my headlights they light up but will not raise, but when I crank them up and plug them in they will wind down.  This is on an 86.    Any ideas??<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000001||jlruiz67||03-18-2001||02:09 AM||||I had that problem with my 87 and I got the kit from rodney dickman. He does have a kit for 86 also.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005633.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005633.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||03-18-2001||02:32 AM||||sounds to me like you have a relay problem....unless it's a striped gear, but if you can use the manual crank then I would assume that's not the case. BTW jlruiz67 the 87-88 headlights used a different electrical system from the 86, although it can be adapted to the 84-86 Fiero. I'd first check out the relay located on the left fender wall since that one controls both motors, if you have one working and the other not, then check more than likely it's the relay located near the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||crzyone||03-18-2001||03:00 AM|||| thanks alot, I'll try replacing the relay<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000004||overlord||03-18-2001||09:28 AM||||ya, sounds like a relay.<BR>same thing happened to mine after i replaced a motor.  Replaced the relay and works fine now.||||reg||1
